# Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) if you need to override a default.
#
# Vite loads `.env*` from THIS directory — the Vite project root — not from the repo root, and only
# variables prefixed `VITE_` are exposed to the bundle. Everything here is public by construction:
# Vite performs a static text replacement of `import.meta.env.VITE_*` at build time, so the value
# ships inside the JavaScript. **Never put a credential behind that prefix.** If something needs a
# key, it goes through the Worker. The full inventory is `.env.example` at the repo root and
# docs/10 "Configuration & secrets".
#
# This app is the WP4-1 renderer proof (one screen, Nearby). It shipped in Wave 4 reading
# `VITE_API_URL` with no `.env.example` beside it and no row in docs/10's table — both fixed in
# Wave 5, which is the whole argument for keeping the inventory in one place.

# Base URL of the edge Worker. Defaults to `DEFAULT_API_URL` in `@nextbus/api-client`
# (`http://localhost:8787`) when unset, which is what `pnpm dev:edge` serves. The socket URL for
# `/v1/live` is *derived* from this value, never configured separately (ADR-056 decision 8).
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8787

# The socket, both read since WP5-6 (ADR-076). `LIVE_TRANSPORT` is `socket` (the shipped default since
# ADR-121, supervised so it degrades to polling on a network that cannot carry WebSockets — ADR-135) or
# `poll`; there is no `auto` spelling, and an unrecognised value falls back to the default with a
# warning. `LIVE_URL` is the escape hatch for a socket tier on a different host — unset means it is
# derived from the API URL above:
# VITE_LIVE_URL=wss://live.example.test/v1/live
# VITE_LIVE_TRANSPORT=poll
